  "reason": "The range identity makes L+μ bijective with inverse K_μ. In the complex branch, coercivity of a_μ±i(·,·) gives full ranges of L+μ±i and the self-adjoint range criterion applies. In the real branch, symmetry plus surjectivity proves real self-adjointness; the canonical isometric complexification is then shown self-adjoint directly. For bounded Ω, K_μ is compact and the resolvent identity factors every complex resolvent through this compact inverse, including the real-operator complexification.",
